  "caption": "Quinn finished a marathon, crab-walked down the stairs the next day, and by day four was planning a speed session.\n\nRecovery usually takes longer than the soreness suggests. Muscles tend to settle first, while tendons and bone can lag behind, so feeling normal isn't quite the same as being recovered.\n\nWhat often helps: gentle running from about 48 hours rather than total rest, keeping easy runs truly conversational, delaying speed, hills and long runs, and letting your own body set the timeline.\n\nGet assessed for pinpoint bone tenderness, pain on hopping or night pain. A swollen, warm calf or breathlessness (especially after a long flight), or dark tea-coloured urine with severe muscle pain, needs urgent medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
